{
   "id": "ITM-GEN-08008-06",
   "archetype_id": "BC-QA-08008",
   "variant_id": "BC-QV-08008-01",
   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = - 2 x^{2} + 5 x + 3 \\) and \\( g(x) = 1 - x \\). The shaded region R shown is bounded by the graphs of f and g and the vertical lines \\( x = 0 \\) and \\( x = 3 \\). Find the exact area of R.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 15
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "On \\( [0, 3] \\), \\( f(x) - g(x) = - 2 x^{2} + 6 x + 2 \\), which is positive, so f is the upper curve and the limits are the given vertical lines.",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99059",
         "rule_named": "upper minus lower"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{0}^{3} \\left(- 2 x^{2} + 6 x + 2\\right)\\,dx \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "area between curves"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "An antiderivative of the integrand is \\( - \\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} + 3 x^{2} + 2 x \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99003",
         "rule_named": "power rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluating from \\( 0 \\) to \\( 3 \\), the area is \\( 15 \\).",
         "mathjson": 15,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"
      }
   ],
   "options": [
